<title>BRAZIL: Brazil house approves Bolivia gas pipeline.</title>
<headline>Brazil house approves Bolivia gas pipeline.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Lower House Thursday gave the go-ahead to a $2.0 billion gas pipeline between Brazil and Bolivia, ratifying an accord between the two countries, officials said.</p>
<p>The project, which has been on the drawing board for 30 years, must now be approved by the Senate.</p>
<p>Due to be funded 75 percent by Brazil and 25 percent by Bolivia, the gasoduct will connect Bolivia with Brazil's centersouth region. The 2,857 km-long pipeline will run through seven Brazilian states.</p>
<p>--Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
</text>
